#N canvas 30 30 2400 1200 12;
#X text 20 20 PGM Probe -- Phase 9 Step 0B. IS Pd's pgmout 0-BASED OR 1-BASED ON THE WIRE? Every test that proved the Volca receives Program Change sent RAW 0xC0 bytes \, which are wire numbers. If pgmout adds or subtracts one \, every patch m_volca selects is off by one and NOTHING reports it -- the 47+n failure shape exactly \, items 190 and 226., f 80;
#X text 900 20 THE READOUT IS BINARY \, WHICH IS WHY IT IS BUILT THIS WAY. This patch sends pgmout 20 every six seconds \, forever. From the shell \, aplaymidi sends RAW 0xC0 20 to the sequencer port in between. IF THE VOLCA'S DISPLAY NEVER CHANGES \, pgmout passes the number straight through and 20 means 20. IF IT FLIPS BACK AND FORTH \, the two paths disagree and pgmout is off by one. Nobody has to read or remember a program NAME -- only whether the name moves., f 80;
#X text 1750 20 WHY NOT JUST COMPARE TWO NAMES. Because that asks a person to hold one name in their head while a second is produced \, and item 226 is the record of three reasoned answers failing where a direct observation succeeded. Did-it-move is the cheapest true question available., f 62;
#X obj 20 340 loadbang;
#X obj 20 390 t b b;
#X msg 20 450 49;
#X msg 240 450 49;
#X obj 700 340 loadbang;
#X obj 700 390 del 2000;
#X obj 700 440 metro 6000;
#X obj 700 500 t b b b;
#X msg 700 570 symbol PGMOUT-21;
#X obj 700 630 s screenLine1;
#X msg 1080 570 21;
#X obj 1080 700 pgmout;
#X obj 1400 570 del 1500;
#X msg 1400 630 48;
#X obj 1400 700 makenote 100 400;
#X obj 1400 780 noteout;
#X text 20 520 THE CHANNEL GOES IN COLD AT LOAD \, off a trigger \, so both destinations hold 49 before any value can arrive. 49 is the Volca's own channel 1 -- Pd input/output slot 4 \, the USB Uno interface. Pd 0.49 does NOT warn about a wrong or missing channel \, so a clean load proves nothing at all and the cold set is what makes it real., f 56;
#X text 700 880 THE TRIGGER'S RIGHTMOST OUTLET WRITES THE SCREEN FIRST \, then the program change goes \, then the note is scheduled 1500 ms behind it. The note exists ONLY so that a still display can be told apart from a dead patch -- if you can hear it and the name is not moving \, that is a real result rather than a hung probe., f 70;
#X text 1400 880 makenote OWNS THE NOTE-OFFS \, so swapping the patch out mid-run cannot leave the Volca droning. 400 ms is long enough to hear which patch is loaded and short enough never to overlap the next cycle., f 60;
#X text 20 760 ⚠️ NOT A DEPLOYED PATCH AND NOT PART OF Cut It. It is a menu patch so that measuring pgmout costs no killall pd -- which strands the Launchpad in Programmer Mode every time \, item 96. Load Cut It again from the menu when done., f 56;
